.TH "json_get_int" "3" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server library"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

int json_get_int(const char *json, const char *key, int *value);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extracts the integer value associated with \f[CR]key\f[R] from a JSON
object string.
Searches for the pattern \f[CR]\(dqkey\(dq:N\f[R] using
\f[CR]strstr(3)\f[R], then converts the numeric portion using
\f[CR]atoi(3)\f[R].
.PP
The function accepts both positive and negative integers (values
starting with \f[CR]\-\f[R] or a digit).
.PP
This is a minimal JSON parser designed for the flat JSON objects used in
the bash\-server protocol.
It does not traverse nested objects.
