.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \f[B]0\f[R] on success, with \f[CR]*value\f[R] set to the
extracted integer.
.PP
Returns \f[B]\-1\f[R] if the key is not found or the value is not a
number.
.SH ERRORS
Returns \-1 when:
.IP \(bu 2
The key is not found in the JSON string.
.IP \(bu 2
The character after \f[CR]\(dqkey\(dq:\f[R] (skipping whitespace) is
neither a digit nor \f[CR]\-\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The key name exceeds 253 characters.
