.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Uses \f[CR]atoi(3)\f[R] for conversion, which does not detect overflow
or invalid trailing characters.
For the bash\-server protocol, integer values are small (channel IDs,
exit codes, levels) so this is adequate.
.IP \(bu 2
The search uses the same \f[CR]strstr(3)\f[R] approach as
\f[CR]json_get_string(3)\f[R].
See the notes on that function regarding potential false matches in
string values.
.IP \(bu 2
The key search buffer is limited to 256 bytes.
.IP \(bu 2
Boolean values (\f[CR]true\f[R], \f[CR]false\f[R]) and \f[CR]null\f[R]
are not matched by this function.
Use \f[CR]json_get_bool()\f[R] (internal, not exported) for booleans.
.IP \(bu 2
Floating\-point values will be truncated to integer by
\f[CR]atoi(3)\f[R].
